r=rule('cambodia-eco-scope','Cambodia’s electronic origin certificates concern exported goods','products-supply','Adding Cambodian goods to a U.S. service or brand offer','The September 2026 official announcement reports electronic Certificates of Origin through the CO Automation System. Determine whether an actual shipment needs origin documentation under the relevant scheme; an e-CO system is not U.S. import or product approval.',[sid['cambodia']],['SKU/specification list','Origin evidence and scheme','Exporter and U.S. importer responsibilities'],exceptions='Full Law on Rules of Origin, five Prakas, commodity measures and U.S. import treatment are not fully reviewed in this guide.')
guide('Cambodia','cambodia','Taking a Cambodian service brand to the U.S.: keep goods-origin evidence separate','Handle Cambodia’s 2026 electronic-origin change without treating a brand licence as a shipment or a certificate as U.S. permission.',[
 sec('Separate three offers before quoting',['A Cambodian service business may be selling know-how, ongoing support and physical supplies in the same commercial proposal. Split those deliverables first. Cambodia’s official September 2026 report describes a new electronic Certificate of Origin system. That change matters to the goods-origin file; it does not by itself classify a U.S. relationship or authorise the product in America.'],sources=[sid['cambodia']]),
 sec('What the origin announcement establishes',['The state agency reports use of co.moc.gov.kh for electronic certificates under preferential and non-preferential schemes. It also identifies implementing Prakas and an FTA portal. This review did not verify the complete instruments or a product-specific preference. A certificate records origin under an applicable process; it is not a universal tariff exemption.'],sources=[sid['cambodia']]),
 sec('Fictional example: training plus a branded maintenance kit',['A Cambodian training and technical-services business proposes a U.S. licensed operator. Remote instruction is one workstream. Replacement components made by several suppliers are another. The COO should not describe the whole kit as Cambodian-origin merely because it is packed in Phnom Penh.','Create a bill of materials and supplier-origin record for each item; let the importer and customs advisers determine the actual origin and tariff treatment. In parallel, test whether the U.S. operator can provide the service using a documented local substitute. Preserve any change to safety, performance and brand standards. These are planning questions, not invented approval requirements.']),
 sec('Build the goods-and-rights schedule',table=(['Deliverable','Evidence owner','Open question'],[['Brand/manual licence','Brand lead','Who owns and may sublicense each right?'],['Remote training/support','COO','Who delivers, updates and handles failures?'],['Physical kit or equipment','Supply lead','What is each item, supplier and supported origin?'],['U.S. import and use','U.S. operating lead','Who is importer; which product/sector rules apply?']])),
 sec('Actions before promising landed costs',bullets=['Supply lead: obtain the current origin-law/Prakas process for the exact goods and retain supplier records.','CFO: keep goods prices, service fees and royalty payments distinct for tax and cash modelling.','Brand lead: check U.S. brand clearance and the scope of existing supplier/IP rights; home registrations are not a U.S. clearance.','Expansion lead: validate a customer specification and domestic substitute before making a territory or supply commitment.','People lead: create a separate mobility task only if someone will work physically in the U.S.; the company address does not determine nationality.'])
 ],[sid['cambodia'],'fed-e2'],[r,'fed-e2-nationality'],'A deliverable-level rights, goods-origin and importer responsibility schedule.',limits=['The current official announcement was read, not all five implementing Prakas. Exact origin procedures, fees, deadlines and U.S. commodity treatment remain unverified. Cambodia is not listed in the reviewed State E-treaty table; personal nationality/other immigration routes remain separate.'])
